{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Vision Transformers (ViT) Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Patch embedding"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn as nn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class PatchEmbedding(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, in_channels=3, patch_size=16, dim=192, image_size=64):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        assert image_size % patch_size == 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.proj = nn.Conv2d(in_channels, dim, kernel_size=patch_size, stride=patch_size)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        num_patches = (image_size // patch_size) ** 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.num_patches = num_patches"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = self.proj(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return x.flatten(2).transpose(1, 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "One conv, one flatten, one transpose. That is the entire image-to-tokens step."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Transformer block"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Pre-LN, multi-head self-attention, MLP with GELU, residual connections."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Block(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, dim, num_heads, mlp_ratio=4, dropout=0.0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.ln1 = nn.LayerNorm(dim)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.attn = nn.MultiheadAttention(dim, num_heads, dropout=dropout, batch_first=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.ln2 = nn.LayerNorm(dim)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.mlp = nn.Sequential("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(dim, dim * mlp_ratio),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.GELU(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Dropout(dropout),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(dim * mlp_ratio, dim),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Dropout(dropout),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        a, _ = self.attn(self.ln1(x), self.ln1(x), self.ln1(x), need_weights=False)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = x + a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = x + self.mlp(self.ln2(x))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`nn.MultiheadAttention` handles the splitting into heads, the scaled dot-product, and the output projection. `batch_first=True` so shapes are `(N, seq, dim)`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: The ViT"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class ViT(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, image_size=64, patch_size=16, in_channels=3,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                 num_classes=10, dim=192, depth=6, num_heads=3, mlp_ratio=4):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.patch = PatchEmbedding(in_channels, patch_size, dim, image_size)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        num_patches = self.patch.num_patches"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.cls_token = nn.Parameter(torch.zeros(1, 1, dim))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.pos_embed = nn.Parameter(torch.zeros(1, num_patches + 1, dim))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.blocks = nn.ModuleList(["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            Block(dim, num_heads, mlp_ratio) for _ in range(depth)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.ln = nn.LayerNorm(dim)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.head = nn.Linear(dim, num_classes)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        nn.init.trunc_normal_(self.pos_embed, std=0.02)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        nn.init.trunc_normal_(self.cls_token, std=0.02)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = self.patch(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        cls = self.cls_token.expand(x.size(0), -1, -1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = torch.cat([cls, x], dim=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = x + self.pos_embed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for blk in self.blocks:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            x = blk(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = self.ln(x[:, 0])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.head(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "vit = ViT(image_size=64, patch_size=16, num_classes=10, dim=192, depth=6, num_heads=3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "x = torch.randn(2, 3, 64, 64)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"output: {vit(x).shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"params: {sum(p.numel() for p in vit.parameters()):,}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "About 2.8M parameters \u2014 a tiny ViT tractable on CPU. Real ViT-B is 86M; same class definition with `dim=768, depth=12, num_heads=12`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Sanity check \u2014 single image inference"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "logits = vit(torch.randn(1, 3, 64, 64))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"logits: {logits}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"probs:  {logits.softmax(-1)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Should run without error. Probabilities sum to 1."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **(Easy)** Print the shapes of every intermediate tensor for a forward pass through the tiny ViT above. Confirm: input `(N, 3, 64, 64)` -> patches `(N, 16, 192)` -> with CLS `(N, 17, 192)` -> classifier input `(N, 192)` -> output `(N, num_classes)`.\n2. **(Medium)** Fine-tune a pretrained `timm` ViT-S/16 on the synthetic-CIFAR dataset from Lesson 4. Compare against ResNet-18 fine-tuning on the same data. Report training time and final accuracy.\n3. **(Hard)** Implement MAE pretraining for the tiny ViT: mask 75% of patches, train the encoder + a small decoder to reconstruct the masked patches. Evaluate linear-probe accuracy on the synthetic data before and after pretraining."
      ]
    }
